{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/111418-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-packs","id":111418,"title":"Idigam Chronicles Weekly Discussion: Packs","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-04-12T05:47:06-07:00","id":111418,"title":"Idigam Chronicles Weekly Discussion: Packs","content":"<a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forsaken-saturday/\" target=\"_blank\">Hail, hail, the gang's all here!</a><br /> <br /> So, this week we get a sneak preview on the subject of Packs, and it's everything I wanted and more! You want violent street gangs? You got it! You want quiet conspiracies? You got it! You want a whole freaking church bowing down your totem? YOU GOT IT<br /> <br /> YOU GET A PACK AND YOU GET A PACK!!<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://stream1.gifsoup.com/view/671944/oprah-you-get-a-car-o.gif\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> Ahem.<br /> <br /> But yes, humans (knowingly or unknowingly), wolf bloods and werewolves alike can get in on the action, which has some really cool implications for different moods between chronicles.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/209-that-other-guy","name":"That Other Guy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-12T05:56:02-07:00","id":111421,"title":"","content":"I was surprised by mother wolf and father luna there seemingly spirits are now mroe spiritlike when it comes to gender^^","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/914-ryu","name":"Ryu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-12T05:58:05-07:00","id":111424,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ryu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/111418-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-packs?p=111421#post111421\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was surprised by mother wolf and father luna there seemingly spirits are now mroe spiritlike when it comes to gender^^</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't notice that - really cool!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/209-that-other-guy","name":"That Other Guy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-12T07:19:21-07:00","id":111453,"title":"","content":"Is it just me, or are they seriously tearing away as much of the Apocalypse-inspired stuff from WtF as they can? XD<br /> <br /> But yeah, I like this a lot. Forsaken is a game about packs, not societies. So it makes perfect sense that they would pack with who they felt was a good fit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-12T07:22:15-07:00","id":111458,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/111418-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-packs?p=111453#post111453\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it just me, or are they seriously tearing away as much of the Apocalypse-inspired stuff from WtF as they can? XD</div> </div> </div> </div>That is exactly what they are doing. Part of the problem with Forsaken was it felt like Apocalypse lite rather than a brand new game<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/444-dessembrae","name":"Dessembrae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar444_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-12T07:24:23-07:00","id":111459,"title":"","content":"Dess, we both lost. ;_; *hugs*<br /> <br /> But on the other hand, we both win! YAY!*goes to read the post*","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-12T07:34:33-07:00","id":111463,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/111418-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-packs?p=111453#post111453\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But yeah, I like this a lot. Forsaken is a game about packs, not societies. So it makes perfect sense that they would pack with who they felt was a good fit.</div> </div> </div> </div>It offers a lot of options. I can see a fair few familial packs floating about, with new members joining and old ones dying down the generations, due to that shared culture, but they don't have to be Crazy Backwoods Folk since they can have their 'pet' humans and wolf-blooded.<br /> <br /> Of course, the big crossover question is &quot;can other supernaturals join packs&quot; :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/209-that-other-guy","name":"That Other Guy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-12T07:35:13-07:00","id":111464,"title":"","content":"I wonder if wolves (or other pets) can be packmates. These new packs are indeed families; but they\u2019re not <i>blood</i> families (unless the pack founders choose for all or most packmates to have blood ties) \u2014 and I know of a number of people who think of their pets as part of the family. And I could see totem-enhanced wolves (for example) serving as scouts and sentries for a pack.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-12T07:59:51-07:00","id":111479,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>That Other Guy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/111418-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-packs?p=111463#post111463\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It offers a lot of options. I can see a fair few familial packs floating about, with new members joining and old ones dying down the generations, due to that shared culture, but they don't have to be Crazy Backwoods Folk since they can have their 'pet' humans and wolf-blooded.<br /> <br /> Of course, the big crossover question is &quot;can other supernaturals join packs&quot; :P</div> </div> </div> </div>If humans, can, I imagine supernaturals theoretically could, but it'd be exceedingly rare. If they DO know it's a supernatural, they'd likely be very suspicious about bringing one out of their own group and into theirs, and if they DON&quot;T, when the totem inevitably mentions 'hey that guy can do magic/isn't alive/etc' they'd probably not be let in because of not being truthful, and maybe treated as a spy.<br /> <br /> That being said, I see it as something that should likely be mechanically allowable, just not common by any stretch. But that's just my guess/what i'd go with if it was up to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-12T08:00:03-07:00","id":111480,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dessembrae</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/111418-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-packs?p=111458#post111458\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is exactly what they are doing. Part of the problem with Forsaken was it felt like Apocalypse lite rather than a brand new game</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I agree. It is really clear how much having to please former-Apocalypse players affected Forsaken, when you see how much they are changing now. Plus, having both lines published now means you cannot say they are trying to remake WtA with WtF (yes, I've heard that).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>That Other Guy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/111418-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-packs?p=111463#post111463\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It offers a lot of options. I can see a fair few familial packs floating about, with new members joining and old ones dying down the generations, due to that shared culture, but they don't have to be Crazy Backwoods Folk since they can have their 'pet' humans and wolf-blooded.<br /> <br /> Of course, the big crossover question is &quot;can other supernaturals join packs&quot; :P</div> </div> </div> </div>It goes into the actual nature of wolf packs, in my opinion. Actual wolf packs are families, with siblings, aunts and uncles and mum and dad. And so, now with Uratha having the ability to breed with other uratha, the packs can function like that. Since some kids are ot born uratha, nor wolf-blood, they now can be as much part of the pack as the rest.<br /> <br /> That, and with that freedom to have non-uratha, it means packs can manifest in interesting ways. Maybe a pack of Iron Masters is like an Anarchist or Greenpeace group that attacks companies. While a Hunters in the Darkness pack could easily include a coven of Wiccans or other pagan groups. We could easily also have a group of business men.<br /> <br /> But the main role is still family, because otherwise the human/wolf-blooded would be allies or contacts, not packmates.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-12T08:16:09-07:00","id":111494,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/111418-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-packs?p=111453#post111453\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it just me, or are they seriously tearing away as much of the Apocalypse-inspired stuff from WtF as they can? XD</div> </div> </div> </div>For my part, I'm just trying to make Forsaken as good a game as it can possibly be on its own merits <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I was never an Apocalypse player in the first place!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-12T08:56:25-07:00","id":111520,"title":"","content":"So, what do I think of new packs? Well, to be fair, the basic premise of this was presented last week, so it's not a new concept. But that said...<br /> <br /> FUCK YEAH, WEREWOLVES ARE NOW OCCULTIC FIGURES! Werewolves, more so than any other supernatural template(save Promethean), have missed out on the sense of being the center of mystical attention, as keystones of a cult, normally because of that entire &quot;Herd Must Not Know&quot; thing. This has steadily started becoming a real downer since with the release of Mummy, human involvement in monstrous affairs has been a growing matter, even if 'Cult' isn't a Blood and Smoke merit directly, But now it's changed-the Uratha can play as anything from the wolf-headed demigods they were in Bau to fellows in a mass of sharp toothed individuals. I said it last week, and I say it again-I love cult/gangs, and I particularly love the earlier mentioned affair of werewolves holding 'mass' in a church, paying chiminage to the totem.(It doesn't hurt that I caught up on Gunnerkrigg Court and found Coyote's true form very Forsaken)<br /> <br /> I'm having a thought towards Kyoko Sakura from Madoka Magica, but that's neither here nor there.<br /> <br /> We didn't talk about the mechanics of packs, but I'm assuming that totem's will be cleaned up from a proto-krewe mechanic to a post-krewe refinement(yes, talking about GtSE here), which will be much appreciated-I never actually liked the base totem rules. My only question is if humans in a pack receive benefits-I imagine they will, but confirmation is a nice thing.<br /> <br /> WEREWOLVES HAVE TOUCHSTONES! <i>WEREWOLVES HAVE TOUCHSTONES!</i> FUCK YES!<br /> <br /> I really like the Touchstone mechanic, both as a mechanic and as a necessary character narrative element. I really despise the idea that a character is alone and associates with no one and in particular has no ties to their own lives. Touchstones were a smart way of counteracting that train of thought and make WoD games more a game of relationships through mechanical benefits. I was hoping they'd be a thing from Vampire on, and it looks like they are. The fact that werewolves can have them both ways is also really neat.<br /> <br /> Ugh, I had more to say but I got lost in a Legend of Zelda convo. Oh well. Anyways, very much approve of this post.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-12T09:59:29-07:00","id":111577,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>falco1029</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/111418-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-packs?p=111479#post111479\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If humans, can, I imagine supernaturals theoretically could, but it'd be exceedingly rare. If they DO know it's a supernatural, they'd likely be very suspicious about bringing one out of their own group and into theirs, and if they DON&quot;T, when the totem inevitably mentions 'hey that guy can do magic/isn't alive/etc' they'd probably not be let in because of not being truthful, and maybe treated as a spy.<br /> <br /> That being said, I see it as something that should likely be mechanically allowable, just not common by any stretch. But that's just my guess/what i'd go with if it was up to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think some supernaturals have more of a precedent for joining a Pack then others and these supernaturals could theoretically work within a Pack.<br /> <br /> Sure beings like Vampires, Changelings, Mummys and Demons who have little direct interaction with Spirits and Spirit phenomena are not likely to join a Pack. As they know far less then Werewolves about Spirits and the Shadow and likely don't have the tools needed to directly hunt such beings.<br /> <br /> I can see a place for a Spirit Mage (Thyrsus likely) in such a group, as while his own knowledge of Spirits and the Shadow will be different from that of the Werewolves, he can bring an alternate point of view to affairs that might be useful to the Pack. Likewise, he has abilities that allow him to contribute to the hunt in some fashion.<br /> <br /> The same applies to the Ulgan lineage of Prometheans could work in a similar way. Particularly one following the refinement of Silver (ironically) that's allowing him to mimic Spirit and Werewolf abilities. The ST would likely have to rule that the Totem bond did something to blunt Disquiet to really make it work, but its not impossible.<br /> <br /> Hunter groups that deal with the possessed and Spirits but don't count Werewolves in their target list could also work. At current I don't think any of the Compacts or Conspiracies quite fit. Ultimately though a tier 1 cell of Hunters could easily be part of the more &quot;extended&quot; pack of humans, as they see the Wolves as a more efficient way to guard against Spirit related stuff.<br /> <br /> Finally, we have Sin-Eaters, who obviously have little to do with Spirits and the Shadow. However, they pretty much mirror the Wolves for dealing with the dead. So I can see a mutual agreement situation coming along of the Sin-Eaters being part of an extended pack (fitting the same role as the humans for the most part) and the Wolves being sorta extended Krewe. They cross-reference stuff with one another to figure out if its Underworld or Shadow related and then they have a wider support network to deal with this stuff in the area.<br /> <br /> That's just my thoughts on the subject. I find trying to add all the Shadow/Spirit stuff to Changeling and Mummy to be problematic in that it makes the setting a little over-complex for me. Vampire's themes are, in my opinion, the most &quot;mundane&quot; of any of the games (including Hunter) and I think adding &quot;other realms&quot; to that equation only degrades that feeling and the wider themes of Vampire. Demon has one power that interacts with the Shadow and frankly the God-Machine and the whole Cover idea present in Demon does not really play well with Werewolf I think. Bad enough to be dealing with Spirit all the time, adding Hunter Angels to the mix is just a bridge to far for me.<br /> <br /> So I guess I agree with Falco in the end. Some other Supernaturals work better then others. The occurrence should not be common at all and like all crossover it should either be used to highlight and interesting point of convergence between the games or should be used to purely for world building.<br /> <br /> (Weirdly I've always felt Promethean crosses over very well with Werewolf, but that's just a mental quirk of mine.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-12T10:16:46-07:00","id":111592,"title":"","content":"All I want now is being able to get literally spirit broods as part of your pack. Think of it as a shared Spiritual Dominance merit, the stuff they showed in the Lone Wolf ruleset.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-12T10:25:08-07:00","id":111597,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hawthorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/111418-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-packs?p=111577#post111577\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think some supernaturals have more of a precedent for joining a Pack then others and these supernaturals could theoretically work within a Pack.<br /> <br /> Sure beings like Vampires, Changelings, Mummys and Demons who have little direct interaction with Spirits and Spirit phenomena are not likely to join a Pack. As they know far less then Werewolves about Spirits and the Shadow and likely don't have the tools needed to directly hunt such beings.<br /> <br /> I can see a place for a Spirit Mage (Thyrsus likely) in such a group, as while his own knowledge of Spirits and the Shadow will be different from that of the Werewolves, he can bring an alternate point of view to affairs that might be useful to the Pack. Likewise, he has abilities that allow him to contribute to the hunt in some fashion.<br /> <br /> The same applies to the Ulgan lineage of Prometheans could work in a similar way. Particularly one following the refinement of Silver (ironically) that's allowing him to mimic Spirit and Werewolf abilities. The ST would likely have to rule that the Totem bond did something to blunt Disquiet to really make it work, but its not impossible.<br /> <br /> Hunter groups that deal with the possessed and Spirits but don't count Werewolves in their target list could also work. At current I don't think any of the Compacts or Conspiracies quite fit. Ultimately though a tier 1 cell of Hunters could easily be part of the more &quot;extended&quot; pack of humans, as they see the Wolves as a more efficient way to guard against Spirit related stuff.<br /> <br /> Finally, we have Sin-Eaters, who obviously have little to do with Spirits and the Shadow. However, they pretty much mirror the Wolves for dealing with the dead. So I can see a mutual agreement situation coming along of the Sin-Eaters being part of an extended pack (fitting the same role as the humans for the most part) and the Wolves being sorta extended Krewe. They cross-reference stuff with one another to figure out if its Underworld or Shadow related and then they have a wider support network to deal with this stuff in the area.<br /> <br /> That's just my thoughts on the subject. I find trying to add all the Shadow/Spirit stuff to Changeling and Mummy to be problematic in that it makes the setting a little over-complex for me. Vampire's themes are, in my opinion, the most &quot;mundane&quot; of any of the games (including Hunter) and I think adding &quot;other realms&quot; to that equation only degrades that feeling and the wider themes of Vampire. Demon has one power that interacts with the Shadow and frankly the God-Machine and the whole Cover idea present in Demon does not really play well with Werewolf I think. Bad enough to be dealing with Spirit all the time, adding Hunter Angels to the mix is just a bridge to far for me.<br /> <br /> So I guess I agree with Falco in the end. Some other Supernaturals work better then others. The occurrence should not be common at all and like all crossover it should either be used to highlight and interesting point of convergence between the games or should be used to purely for world building.<br /> <br /> (Weirdly I've always felt Promethean crosses over very well with Werewolf, but that's just a mental quirk of mine.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I entirely agree that some work better than others; a Thyrsus or a Gangrel w/ Blood Tenebrous (or a Dead Wolf if you convert bloodlines for your game) or certain prometheans are likely the best fit. I think GMC makes spirits a little more universal, overall, and it allows for anyone to focus on them as much as any mortal could.<br /> <br /> Past that, I do agree that for others they'd never be any more 'integrated' than a normal human, something like your sin-eater pack/krewe example; go to one or the other if you don't have the skills to deal with ephemera X.<br /> <br /> As for hunters, tier 1 hunts are basically humans, so if werewolves aren't one of their usual targets (or if they know that not all werewolves are 'bad'), they could easily fit into a pack like a human could, perhaps deal with some threats that don't fall under the sacred hunt. That could actually fit well for certain other supernaturals too; a Khaibit is better suited for dealing with Strix if they're bugging humans than a werewolf, I imagine.<br /> <br /> Still, these should be the sorts of things that in any small game might be a one time thing local to the setting, I also agree; you wouldn't expect a hunter compact in every pack, or a mage amongst werewolves in every city.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-12T10:57:59-07:00","id":111611,"title":"","content":"One thing this blog left me wondering... If humans can be part of a werewolf pack, can spirits be too? Other than the totem, I mean. As the blog says, the totem sort of synthesizes with the pack, binding them together. But if a Werewolf's human touchstones can be considered an extended part of the pack, why can't her spirit touchstones be as well? Obviously, only certain spirits would associate and even aid the Uratha by choice, but if a spirit is sympathetic to the pack's goals, why not let it join?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-12T12:48:17-07:00","id":111703,"title":"","content":"Personal totems for Primal Urge 6+ werewolves please.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-12T12:55:07-07:00","id":111710,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dessembrae</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/111418-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-packs?p=111458#post111458\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is exactly what they are doing. Part of the problem with Forsaken was it felt like Apocalypse lite rather than a brand new game</div> </div> </div> </div>Like what Chris said - for my part, when I'm writing my sections, I haven't thought one whit about Apocalypse. The only things I'm thinking are the following:<br /> <br /> 1. &quot;Okay, so if this goes here and does this, what is something interesting that happens?&quot;<br /> 2. &quot;How can I make this creepy/scary/threatening?&quot; (Pick one or more.)<br /> 3. &quot;Man, I hope I can get this all done by deadline.&quot;<br /> <br /> That's about it, other than particulars of my sections that I can't share. To be fair, though, the bulk of what I've worked on to date has been some baddies which have no connection to Apocalypse in the first place, so my brain doesn't go there. Plus, as much as I loved Apocalypse back in the day, I've shoved so much Forsaken into my brain that the Apocalypse information is in my brain's sub-basement. Go down the stairs, to the end of the corridor, behind the barricaded door, fight your way past the leopard, and then look in the bottom drawer of the filing cabinet. The information is taped to the bottom. (First person who tells me where I paraphrased that last bit from gets a drink from me at GenCon, or an internet cookie, whichever is practical.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This space for rent.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/552-strider1276","name":"strider1276","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar552_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"382"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-12T13:24:17-07:00","id":111723,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>strider1276</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/111418-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-packs?p=111710#post111710\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Like what Chris said - for my part, when I'm writing my sections, I haven't thought one whit about Apocalypse. The only things I'm thinking are the following: 1. &amp;quot;Okay, so if this goes here and does this, what is something interesting that happens?&amp;quot; 2. &amp;quot;How can I make this creepy/scary/threatening?&amp;quot; (Pick one or more.) 3. &amp;quot;Man, I hope I can get this all done by deadline.&amp;quot; That's about it, other than particulars of my sections that I can't share. To be fair, though, the bulk of what I've worked on to date has been some baddies which have no connection to Apocalypse in the first place, so my brain doesn't go there. Plus, as much as I loved Apocalypse back in the day, I've shoved so much Forsaken into my brain that the Apocalypse information is in my brain's sub-basement. Go down the stairs, to the end of the corridor, behind the barricaded door, fight your way past the leopard, and then look in the bottom drawer of the filing cabinet. The information is taped to the bottom. (First person who tells me where I paraphrased that last bit from gets a drink from me at GenCon, or an internet cookie, whichever is practical.)</div> </div> </div> </div> Shot in the dark, but reminds me of Dreamcatcher.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-12T13:47:54-07:00","id":111739,"title":"","content":"I would like to know what the non-Uratha members of a pack do when the pack goes to war. Do they take part in the fighting? Do they play a reconnaissance role? Is it a problem for Uratha if <i>someone else </i>uses a silver weapon on their behalf?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/233-daydreamer","name":"Daydreamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar233_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"193"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-12T14:16:14-07:00","id":111754,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Daydreamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/111418-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-packs?p=111739#post111739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would like to know what the non-Uratha members of a pack do when the pack goes to war. Do they take part in the fighting? Do they play a reconnaissance role? Is it a problem for Uratha if <i>someone else </i>uses a silver weapon on their behalf?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would like to believe that they would play to their strengths. If I have a human who is a great scout, I would use him for recon. If I have a wolf-blooded kin who acts as a locus, I may bring him into the know and use him as a mobile gauntlet breach if needed while bringing him along.<br /> <br /> As for a silver weapon, just as currently you aren't held responsible for the actions a packmate does if you tried your hardest to prevent it, should you condone the use of silver weapons and find out later that someone you know used it, I wouldn't consider that a harmony hit. Now if I told them to do it and they did so, then I would rule that you do take a hit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/444-dessembrae","name":"Dessembrae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar444_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-12T14:38:34-07:00","id":111770,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Daydreamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/111418-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-packs?p=111739#post111739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would like to know what the non-Uratha members of a pack do when the pack goes to war. Do they take part in the fighting? Do they play a reconnaissance role? Is it a problem for Uratha if <i>someone else </i>uses a silver weapon on their behalf?</div> </div> </div> </div>Whatever the pack deems they should do, I'd assume.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-12T16:35:13-07:00","id":111817,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/111418-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-packs?p=111464#post111464\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder if wolves (or other pets) can be packmates. These new packs are indeed families; but they\u2019re not <i>blood</i> families (unless the pack founders choose for all or most packmates to have blood ties) \u2014 and I know of a number of people who think of their pets as part of the family. And I could see totem-enhanced wolves (for example) serving as scouts and sentries for a pack.</div> </div> </div> </div>While the book probably won't say anything in regards to this, I would personally allow such a thing provided I feel the connection is strong enough or there is good roleplay motivation to do so. I would allow this as I don't see this as a huge stretch especially in the nWOD's fairly open environment unless it is explicitly stated otherwise. On the other hand, I would definitely rule that giving commands to them would mandate an Uratha having the ability to speak with beasts to do anything more than simple commands such as kill, stay, etc.<br /> <br /> If I want to tell a wolf to go over the hill yonder, wait for the sun to set, and then attack all of the chickens to make a scene, that is well beyond normal communication without the use of a gift.<br /> <br /> That being said, if a player simply says I want a wolf as part of the pack, I will say no without sufficient backstory important to the character. They can't just say &quot;oh...the wolf was his dearest companion and only friend in the world&quot; without the player basing his entire roleplay experience around this fact.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":444,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/444-dessembrae","user":"Dessembrae","date":". 04-12-2014, 07:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/444-dessembrae","name":"Dessembrae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar444_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-12T19:41:03-07:00","id":111875,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/111418-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-packs?p=111723#post111723\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Shot in the dark, but reminds me of Dreamcatcher.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you're talking about the 2003 movie (which came up when I Googled it), then that's not it. Try a bit more British, and a lot funnier. :-)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This space for rent.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/552-strider1276","name":"strider1276","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar552_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"382"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-12T21:07:03-07:00","id":111895,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>strider1276</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/111418-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-packs?p=111875#post111875\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If you're talking about the 2003 movie (which came up when I Googled it), then that's not it. Try a bit more British, and a lot funnier. :-)</div> </div> </div> </div>By default I will need to say Monty Pythons Flying circus, although I admittedly have no clue. It is just the only funny British show I know.<br /> <br /> Switching topics, I am hoping the book goes over what is considered acceptable use of humans and wolf-blooded especially since it is stated that they were never supposed to perform the Sacred Hunt. Knowing this, if they are not supposed to be part of this, then are they merely relegated to &quot;the adults are going out now Timmy, but you can stay with Vicki the babysitter until we come home&quot; type of assistance.<br /> <br /> I did some paraphrasing of my own in the last part as well <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <b>NEW SIDE QUEST:</b> Work some sort of reference into a relevant discussion without sidetracking the topic<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/444-dessembrae","name":"Dessembrae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar444_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-12T21:12:44-07:00","id":111896,"title":"","content":"I would guess that the use of wolf-blooded and humans is going to very much be YMMV. In territories with a lot of Uratha and the hunt under control, the outer pack will cover the more mundane aspects. In territories with few Uratha and a lot of prey, you can bet the wolf-blooded (and maybe even humans) are getting dragged into that Beshilu nest to help sort it out.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-12T21:44:55-07:00","id":111900,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>strider1276</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/111418-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-packs?p=111875#post111875\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If you're talking about the 2003 movie (which came up when I Googled it), then that's not it. Try a bit more British, and a lot funnier. :-)</div> </div> </div> </div>No, the Stephen king novel it was based on. My first instinct with british comedy is monty python, but I know that can't be it. Hitchiker's Guide, then?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-12T22:51:47-07:00","id":111926,"title":"","content":"The leopard is the giveaway for Hitchiker's Guide. Right next to the Planning Office, I presume?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-13T00:19:43-07:00","id":111942,"title":"","content":"Didn't really like the idea of wolf-bloods and humans becoming part of an actual pack, but well for the people who do. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-13T02:18:37-07:00","id":111963,"title":"","content":"Stew had mentioned we'd find out what would replace the breeding taboo this week. I take it he meant Touchstones: the breeding taboo requires werewolves breed with humans to keep the species alive. The Touchstone system means that Uratha are still heavily incentivized if-not-compelled to form connections to human beings rather than avoid the hardship of rage to form connections only with other Uratha. You jeopardize your Harmony by losing touch with humanity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-13T04:47:23-07:00","id":111994,"title":"","content":"Hmm.... so, we can have extended spirits, wolf blooded, and even mundane humans as part of the pack. That's cool - I remember one game where my pack ended up adopting a couple different kinds of various cat spirits, setting up shrines. It'd be fun to have them as officially part of the pack under these rules.<br /> <br /> Well, other than that, well... I don't really see much to say. I dig the pack being more flexible. I like how they're making humans and bloods actually matter to the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 04-13-2014, 07:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-13T05:44:23-07:00","id":112013,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/111418-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-packs?p=111900#post111900\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, the Stephen king novel it was based on. My first instinct with british comedy is monty python, but I know that can't be it. Hitchiker's Guide, then?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, right, that works too. And yes, it's Hitchhiker's Guide to the Galaxy. You and Bunyip each get an internet cookie, or, if you're going to be at GenCon, let me know privately and we'll sort out the whole drink thing.<br /> <br /> Okay, to get back on-topic meow, I've been excited about the pack thing for a while now, and I'm glad so many people like it. Next week, though, you guys get a treat because...Gifts. I think the Gifts were so well done. I am very much looking forward to playtesting based solely on the Gifts section. I mean, that's my personal opinion, so take that for what you will, but I think the execution was brilliant. One of my favorite parts of the book so far. Well, other than mine, of course. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This space for rent.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/552-strider1276","name":"strider1276","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar552_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"382"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-13T07:24:13-07:00","id":112041,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/111418-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-packs?p=111963#post111963\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Stew had mentioned we'd find out what would replace the breeding taboo this week. I take it he meant Touchstones: the breeding taboo requires werewolves breed with humans to keep the species alive. The Touchstone system means that Uratha are still heavily incentivized if-not-compelled to form connections to human beings rather than avoid the hardship of rage to form connections only with other Uratha. You jeopardize your Harmony by losing touch with humanity.</div> </div> </div> </div>Touchstones, certainly; but also the human component of the expanded pack. I presume that there are benefits to having humans in your pack beyond such things as providing you with \u201cBreaking Human\u201d opportunities for your Harmony. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-13T10:58:23-07:00","id":112122,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/111418-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-packs?p=112041#post112041\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I presume that there are benefits to having humans in your pack beyond such things as providing you with \u201cBreaking Human\u201d opportunities for your Harmony.</div> </div> </div> </div>I will let you reread this statement and then come to the inevitable conclusion <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/444-dessembrae","name":"Dessembrae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar444_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-13T13:09:26-07:00","id":112202,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>strider1276</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/111418-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-packs?p=112013#post112013\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, to get back on-topic meow, I've been excited about the pack thing for a while now, and I'm glad so many people like it. Next week, though, you guys get a treat because...Gifts. I think the Gifts were so well done. I am very much looking forward to playtesting based solely on the Gifts section. I mean, that's my personal opinion, so take that for what you will, but I think the execution was brilliant. One of my favorite parts of the book so far. Well, other than mine, of course. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I've been really blown away by the team's reactions to the Gifts; I was a bit worried when I put my first draft up, so the approval has been hugely gratifying <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I have no idea what specifically Stew's going to post up on Friday, but am girding myself for the crucible of public opinion... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-13T14:54:22-07:00","id":112252,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/111418-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-packs?p=112202#post112202\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I've been really blown away by the team's reactions to the Gifts; I was a bit worried when I put my first draft up, so the approval has been hugely gratifying <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I have no idea what specifically Stew's going to post up on Friday, but am girding myself for the crucible of public opinion... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>At least answer us this...was the massive houseruled gift thread that is currently stickied at the top of this forum and was also stickied in the old forum consulted in any part as a basis?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/444-dessembrae","name":"Dessembrae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar444_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-13T15:17:57-07:00","id":112267,"title":"","content":"That's a tricky question because I want to say 'No, but...' and the context that comes after the 'but' is extremely important but also spoilers for stuff Stew will be discussing on Friday. I don't want to give a vague answer but I hope you'll understand.<br /> <br /> You can be assured that I have plenty of experience of, and did plenty of delving into general opinions of, the problems and issues with the old Gift lists. But no, I wasn't consulting the house rules thread for guidance while writing the new Gifts.<br /> <br /> Ask again after the next Forsaken Friday update and I may be able to give you the second half of the answer that comes after 'No, but...' <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-13T16:26:36-07:00","id":112311,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/111418-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-packs?p=112202#post112202\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I've been really blown away by the team's reactions to the Gifts; I was a bit worried when I put my first draft up, so the approval has been hugely gratifying <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I have no idea what specifically Stew's going to post up on Friday, but am girding myself for the crucible of public opinion... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>The praise is very deserving, sir. You saw what happened when I remade one of my old characters' Gift list. The focus tightened up considerably. I was a little worried at first when I made an NPC in my one section, but then I realized I wasn't considering certain options and that cleared up the issue. <br /> <br /> I'm excited to see what Stew shares on Friday, and the fan reaction to it. :-)<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This space for rent.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/552-strider1276","name":"strider1276","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar552_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"382"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-13T16:31:42-07:00","id":112315,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>strider1276</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/111418-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-packs?p=112311#post112311\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm excited to see what Stew shares on Friday, and the fan reaction to it. :-)</div> </div> </div> </div>Permission to time travel to Friday?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/444-dessembrae","name":"Dessembrae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar444_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-13T17:13:39-07:00","id":112329,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dessembrae</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/111418-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-packs?p=112315#post112315\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Permission to time travel to Friday?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry, wrong game line. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This space for rent.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/552-strider1276","name":"strider1276","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar552_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"382"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-13T23:43:36-07:00","id":112455,"title":"","content":"I felt Gifts were the part of the Forsaken core most in need of revisiting and rewriting, hope I'm as pleased with them as you are Strider. The higher level Gifts weren't too bad but the rank 1-2 Gifts didn't do much for me at all, a sentiment shared by my old play group. We just didn't like the way the effects scaled from &quot;fairly useless&quot; to &quot;holy fuck I just destroyed that small town by accident&quot;. We also wanted to see some kind of parity between the equivalent Gift dot levels, not every 5 dot Gift was as impressive or worth the effort to obtain as others, I'm hoping to see that addressed in the final draft as well. Later supplements helped but I don't want to wait for a few supplements before I have a set of Gifts that I like and fit the character I'm playing.<br /> <br /> Since I liked the teased changes to Packs and Tribes I expect to be pretty satisfied with what you guys are doing. Good job so far. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-14T08:24:30-07:00","id":112658,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksider</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/111418-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-packs?p=112455#post112455\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We just didn't like the way the effects scaled from &quot;fairly useless&quot; to &quot;holy fuck I just destroyed that small town by accident&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>You mean to tell me that not all gifts are created equal?! mean it's not like feet of mist was pretty much useless while partial change is almost god-tier for level 1<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/444-dessembrae","name":"Dessembrae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar444_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-14T17:11:10-07:00","id":113023,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/111418-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-packs?p=112267#post112267\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's a tricky question because I want to say 'No, but...' and the context that comes after the 'but' is extremely important but also spoilers for stuff Stew will be discussing on Friday. I don't want to give a vague answer but I hope you'll understand.<br /> <br /> You can be assured that I have plenty of experience of, and did plenty of delving into general opinions of, the problems and issues with the old Gift lists. But no, I wasn't consulting the house rules thread for guidance while writing the new Gifts.<br /> <br /> Ask again after the next Forsaken Friday update and I may be able to give you the second half of the answer that comes after 'No, but...' <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Thank god. That'd be just what we needed, rewrites of rewrites. *shudder*<br /> <br /> I'd much rather see a radical new approach than yet another rehash. If the second half of that answer is what I think it is, I'll be very happy come Friday <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><